{"id":"20260827T220841.380986323Z-06ba411e","time":"2026-08-27T22:08:41.380986323Z","session_id":"session-20260827T220630.639097715Z","task_id":"task-1787868390639244453","source":"architect","kind":"plan.proposed","summary":"Add the received byte count to gosumcheck's existing per-fetch verbose diagnostic while preserving all non-verbose and failure behavior.\n\nPlan:\n  1. Update gosumcheck/main.go documentation and the successful verbose fetch line to emit \"\u003celapsed\u003es \u003cbytes\u003e bytes \u003ctarget\u003e\" using len(data).\n  2. Add gosumcheck/main_test.go with an intercepted HTTP transport and captured stderr to verify the successful verbose line, non-verbose silence, and error-path silence.\n  3. Run go test ./gosumcheck.","payload":{"decision":"proceed","summary":"Add the received byte count to gosumcheck's existing per-fetch verbose diagnostic while preserving all non-verbose and failure behavior.","steps":["Update gosumcheck/main.go documentation and the successful verbose fetch line to emit \"\u003celapsed\u003es \u003cbytes\u003e bytes \u003ctarget\u003e\" using len(data).","Add gosumcheck/main_test.go with an intercepted HTTP transport and captured stderr to verify the successful verbose line, non-verbose silence, and error-path silence.","Run go test ./gosumcheck."],"consequences":"Successful verbose fetches expose response size on the existing single stderr line. Non-verbose executions emit no new output, and transport, HTTP-status, and body-read failures retain their current returns and diagnostics.","files":["gosumcheck/main.go","gosumcheck/main_test.go"],"mode":"modify","plan":"For each successfully completed remote read, retain the single verbose diagnostic line and format it as elapsed time, decimal byte count, and target. Derive the count from the successfully read response data, without moving output into any failure branch. Add a deterministic regression test around ReadRemote and verify the gosumcheck package.","claims":[{"statement":"clientOps.ReadRemote currently emits one stderr line containing elapsed time and target only after a successful body read and only when -v is enabled.","about":"gosumcheck/main.go","source":"repository"},{"statement":"The successfully received body is already stored in data immediately before verbose reporting, so its byte count is available as len(data).","about":"gosumcheck/main.go","source":"repository"},{"statement":"The existing gosumcheck/test.bash invokes verbose mode but does not assert the output format.","about":"gosumcheck/test.bash","source":"repository"},{"statement":"Sensei indexes gosumcheck/main.go and reports this scoped change as low-risk with local blast radius, no approval gate, and no anchored governing rule, required test, failure mode, or forbidden fix.","about":"gosumcheck/main.go","source":"graph"},{"statement":"The proposed gosumcheck/main_test.go does not yet exist and is therefore not indexed by Sensei.","about":"gosumcheck/main_test.go","source":"repository"}],"prospective_surfaces":[{"path":"gosumcheck/main_test.go","package":"main","role":"go-regression-test","dependencies":["io","net/http","os","strings","testing"]}],"plan_source":"architect"}}
